{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "D0LID5", "uniProtkbId": "BMCH_HALO1", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "2021-06-02", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-01-28", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2009-12-15", "entryVersion": 64, "sequenceVersion": 1}, "annotationScore": 3.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Haliangium ochraceum (strain DSM 14365 / JCM 11303 / SMP-2)", "taxonId": 502025, "lineage": ["Bacteria", "Pseudomonadati", "Myxococcota", "Polyangia", "Haliangiales", "Kofleriaceae", "Haliangium"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26617073"}], "value": "Bacterial microcompartment protein homohexamer"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26617073"}], "value": "BMC-H"}]}}, "genes": [{"orderedLocusNames": [{"value": "Hoch_5815"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "28642439"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30833088"}], "value": "The only hexameric shell protein in this bacterium, it forms the majority of the bacterial microcompartment (BMC) shell. Expression of 5 proteins in E.coli (BMC-H (Hoch_5815), BMC-P (Hoch_5814), and 3 BMC-T (Hoch_5812, Hoch_5816, Hoch_3341)) forms a 40 nm artificial BMC with a molecular mass of 6.5 MDa. There are 60 BMC-H hexamers per BMC. The shell facets are 20-30 Angstroms thick (a single hexamer layer), with 1 of BMC-T trimers protruding to the exterior"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26617073"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "28642439"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30833088"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "31075444"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30901520"}], "value": "Homohexamer with a small central pore (Probable) (PubMed:26617073, PubMed:28642439, PubMed:30833088, PubMed:31075444). When purified protein is examined by atomic force microscopy it dynamically makes uniform patches about 35 Angstroms thick with hexamers in the same orientation (PubMed:26617073). In the BMC the concave side faces outward, with the N- and C-terminii exposed to the cytoplasm (PubMed:28642439)"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24631000"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "28642439"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30833088"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30901520"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "31075444"}], "value": "Bacterial microcompartment", "id": "SL-0544"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24631000"}], "value": "Absolutely required for BMC formation; when deleted from an artificial operon (Hoch_5815, Hoch_5812, Hoch_3341, Hoch_5816, Hoch_4425, Hoch_4426, Hoch_5814) being expressed in E.coli, no BMC shells are made"}], "commentType": "DISRUPTION PHENOTYPE"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "24631000"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "28642439"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30901520"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "31075444"}], "value": "Artificial BMCs can be made in E.coli by expressing (Hoch_5815, Hoch_5812, Hoch_3341, Hoch_5816, Hoch_4425, Hoch_4426, Hoch_5814) or (BMC-H (Hoch_5815), BMC-P (Hoch_5814), and 3 BMC-T (Hoch_5812, Hoch_5816, Hoch_3341)). Cargo proteins can be targeted to this BMC (PubMed:24631000, PubMed:28642439). Artificial BMCs can be made by duplicating this gene with a 16 residue linker between the copies (making an artificial BMC-T). The shell assembles into balls with holes where the pentameric subunit would be, and can be used as a model to study assembly and permeability (PubMed:30901520). Additional changes to this protein place the N- and C-terminii in the interior of the shell (called CPH). Fusing proteins to the C-terminus of CPH allows targeting of cargo proteins to the lumen of the organelle composed of CPH, BMC-P and BMC-T1 (PubMed:31075444)"}], "commentType": "BIOTECHNOLOGY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule", "id": "PRU01278"}], "value": "Belongs to the bacterial microcompartments protein family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}], "features": [{"type": "Chain", "location": {"start": {"value": 1, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 99, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Bacterial microcompartment protein homohexamer", "featureId": "PRO_0000452545"}, {"type": "Domain", "location": {"start": {"value": 4, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 88, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "BMC", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000255", "source": "PROSITE-ProRule", "id": "PRU01278"}]}, {"type": "Mutagenesis", "location": {"start": {"value": 28, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 28, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Forms larger hexamer patches, increases hexamer stacking.", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26617073"}], "alternativeSequence": {"originalSequence": "K", "alternativeSequences": ["A"]}}, {"type": "Mutagenesis", "location": {"start": {"value": 78, "modifier": "EXACT"}, "end": {"value": 78, "modifier": "EXACT"}}, "description": "Forms smaller hexamer patches.", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26617073"}], "alternativeSequence": {"originalSequence": "R", "alternativeSequences": ["A"]}}, {"type": "Beta strand", "location": {"